{"type":"message","id":"2cd8bcee","parentId":"262fd139","timestamp":"2026-02-16T14:44:29.586Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking me to start a new session using the default model `kilo/z-ai/glm-5:free` and terminate the current session.\n\nLet me understand what this means:\n1. They want to start a new session with a specific model\n2. They want to terminate the current session\n\nLooking at the runtime info, I can see:\n- Current model: `kilo/z-ai/glm-5:free`\n- Default model: `github-copilot/gpt-4o`\n\nWait, the current model IS already `kilo/z-ai/glm-5:free`. So they're asking to start a new session with the same model that's currently running.\n\nThis is a bit confusing. Let me think about what they might mean:\n1. They want to restart the current session (refresh it)\n2. They want to spawn a new session and terminate this one\n\nAs a subagent, I should complete this task. The task is to \"Start a new session using the default model `kilo/z-ai/glm-5:free` and terminate the current session.\"\n\nLooking at available tools, I don't see a direct tool to start a new session or terminate the current one. However, I can use the `exec` tool to run OpenClaw CLI commands.\n\nFrom the context, I know:\n- OpenClaw has CLI subcommands\n- I should run `openclaw help` if unsure\n\nBut wait - I don't have direct access to openclaw session management commands in my tool descriptions. Let me check what I can do:\n\n1. I could try running `openclaw` commands via `exec`\n2. I could report back that I don't have the capability\n\nActually, looking at the OpenClaw CLI reference, it mentions:\n- `openclaw gateway status/start/stop/restart`\n\nBut it doesn't mention session management. The user is asking me to manage sessions, which might be a higher-level operation.\n\nLet me try to execute an openclaw command to see what options are available. I'll try `openclaw --help` or `openclaw session --help` to understand how to start a new session.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"text","text":"I'll help you start a new session with the specified model. Let me check the available OpenClaw commands for session management."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_a5cb45ce4e9942e0815b09c9","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"openclaw --help"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"kilo","model":"z-ai/glm-5:free","usage":{"input":5066,"output":974,"cacheRead":2944,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":8984,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1771253041183}}
{"type":"message","id":"4bb65abe","parentId":"2cd8bcee","timestamp":"2026-02-16T14:44:33.756Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_a5cb45ce4e9942e0815b09c9","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"🦞 OpenClaw 2026.2.9 (33c75cb) — If you're lost, run doctor; if you're brave, run prod; if you're wise, run tests.\n\nUsage: openclaw [options] [command]\n\nOptions:\n  --dev             Dev profile: isolate state under ~/.openclaw-dev, default\n                    gateway port 19001, and shift derived ports (browser/canvas)\n  -h, --help        display help for command\n  --no-color        Disable ANSI colors\n  --profile <name>  Use a named profile (isolates\n                    OPENCLAW_STATE_DIR/OPENCLAW_CONFIG_PATH under\n                    ~/.openclaw-<name>)\n  -V, --version     output the version number\n\nCommands:\n  acp               Agent Control Protocol tools\n  agent             Run an agent turn via the Gateway (use --local for embedded)\n  agents            Manage isolated agents (workspaces + auth + routing)\n  approvals         Exec approvals\n  browser           Manage OpenClaw's dedicated browser (Chrome/Chromium)\n  channels          Channel management\n  completion        Generate shell completion script\n  config            Config helpers (get/set/unset). Run without subcommand for\n                    the wizard.\n  configure         Interactive prompt to set up credentials, devices, and agent\n                    defaults\n  cron              Cron scheduler\n  daemon            Gateway service (legacy alias)\n  dashboard         Open the Control UI with your current token\n  devices           Device pairing + token management\n  directory         Directory commands\n  dns               DNS helpers\n  docs              Docs helpers\n  doctor            Health checks + quick fixes for the gateway and channels\n  gateway           Gateway control\n  health            Fetch health from the running gateway\n  help              display help for command\n  hooks             Hooks tooling\n  logs              Gateway logs\n  memory            Memory search tools\n  message           Send messages and channel actions\n  models            Model configuration\n  node              Node control\n  nodes             Node commands\n  onboard           Interactive wizard to set up the gateway, workspace, and\n                    skills\n  pairing           Pairing helpers\n  plugins           Plugin management\n  reset             Reset local config/state (keeps the CLI installed)\n  sandbox           Sandbox tools\n  security          Security helpers\n  sessions          List stored conversation sessions\n  setup             Initialize ~/.openclaw/openclaw.json and the agent workspace\n  system            System events, heartbeat, and presence\n  skills            Skills management\n  status            Show channel health and recent session recipients\n  tui               Terminal UI\n  uninstall         Uninstall the gateway service + local data (CLI remains)\n  update            CLI update helpers\n  webhooks          Webhook helpers\n\nExamples:\n  openclaw channels login --verbose\n    Link personal WhatsApp Web and show QR + connection logs.\n  openclaw message send --target +15555550123 --message \"Hi\" --json\n    Send via your web session and print JSON result.\n  openclaw gateway --port 18789\n    Run the WebSocket Gateway locally.\n  openclaw --dev gateway\n    Run a dev Gateway (isolated state/config) on ws://127.0.0.1:19001.\n  openclaw gateway --force\n    Kill anything bound to the default gateway port, then start it.\n  openclaw gateway ...\n    Gateway control via WebSocket.\n  openclaw agent --to +15555550123 --message \"Run summary\" --deliver\n    Talk directly to the agent using the Gateway; optionally send the WhatsApp reply.\n  openclaw message send --channel telegram --target @mychat --message \"Hi\"\n    Send via your Telegram bot.\n\nDocs: https://docs.openclaw.ai/cli"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":4162,"aggregated":"🦞 OpenClaw 2026.2.9 (33c75cb) — If you're lost, run doctor; if you're brave, run prod; if you're wise, run tests.\n\nUsage: openclaw [options] [command]\n\nOptions:\n  --dev             Dev profile: isolate state under ~/.openclaw-dev, default\n                    gateway port 19001, and shift derived ports (browser/canvas)\n  -h, --help        display help for command\n  --no-color        Disable ANSI colors\n  --profile <name>  Use a named profile (isolates\n                    OPENCLAW_STATE_DIR/OPENCLAW_CONFIG_PATH under\n                    ~/.openclaw-<name>)\n  -V, --version     output the version number\n\nCommands:\n  acp               Agent Control Protocol tools\n  agent             Run an agent turn via the Gateway (use --local for embedded)\n  agents            Manage isolated agents (workspaces + auth + routing)\n  approvals         Exec approvals\n  browser           Manage OpenClaw's dedicated browser (Chrome/Chromium)\n  channels          Channel management\n  completion        Generate shell completion script\n  config            Config helpers (get/set/unset). Run without subcommand for\n                    the wizard.\n  configure         Interactive prompt to set up credentials, devices, and agent\n                    defaults\n  cron              Cron scheduler\n  daemon            Gateway service (legacy alias)\n  dashboard         Open the Control UI with your current token\n  devices           Device pairing + token management\n  directory         Directory commands\n  dns               DNS helpers\n  docs              Docs helpers\n  doctor            Health checks + quick fixes for the gateway and channels\n  gateway           Gateway control\n  health            Fetch health from the running gateway\n  help              display help for command\n  hooks             Hooks tooling\n  logs              Gateway logs\n  memory            Memory search tools\n  message           Send messages and channel actions\n  models            Model configuration\n  node              Node control\n  nodes             Node commands\n  onboard           Interactive wizard to set up the gateway, workspace, and\n                    skills\n  pairing           Pairing helpers\n  plugins           Plugin management\n  reset             Reset local config/state (keeps the CLI installed)\n  sandbox           Sandbox tools\n  security          Security helpers\n  sessions          List stored conversation sessions\n  setup             Initialize ~/.openclaw/openclaw.json and the agent workspace\n  system            System events, heartbeat, and presence\n  skills            Skills management\n  status            Show channel health and recent session recipients\n  tui               Terminal UI\n  uninstall         Uninstall the gateway service + local data (CLI remains)\n  update            CLI update helpers\n  webhooks          Webhook helpers\n\nExamples:\n  openclaw channels login --verbose\n    Link personal WhatsApp Web and show QR + connection logs.\n  openclaw message send --target +15555550123 --message \"Hi\" --json\n    Send via your web session and print JSON result.\n  openclaw gateway --port 18789\n    Run the WebSocket Gateway locally.\n  openclaw --dev gateway\n    Run a dev Gateway (isolated state/config) on ws://127.0.0.1:19001.\n  openclaw gateway --force\n    Kill anything bound to the default gateway port, then start it.\n  openclaw gateway ...\n    Gateway control via WebSocket.\n  openclaw agent --to +15555550123 --message \"Run summary\" --deliver\n    Talk directly to the agent using the Gateway; optionally send the WhatsApp reply.\n  openclaw message send --channel telegram --target @mychat --message \"Hi\"\n    Send via your Telegram bot.\n\nDocs: https://docs.openclaw.ai/cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\Raitis\\.openclaw\\workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1771253073752}}
